gsipper (1.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Pre-compiled codecs bundled in the .deb: Opus, G.722, G.711
    a-law / µ-law, G.729 (via libbcg729) and GSM Full-Rate, in
    addition to the existing G.726-32. The default codec priority
    list (Account > Advanced > Codecs) now leads with Opus.
  * build.sh PJ_BUILD_DEPS gains libbcg729-dev so a local
    './build.sh --pjsua2' picks up G.729 automatically.
  * debian/control.in Depends gain libbcg729-0 and libgsm1 so the
    bundled _pjsua2.so loads on the target without further apt
    installs.
  * SILK is intentionally not built — it requires Skype's SILK SDK,
    which is not in Debian repositories.
  * README: drop the MicroSIP reference in the tagline; gsipper is
    described straight as a modern native GNOME SIP client.

 -- pulpoff <noreply@pulpoff.com>  Tue, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

gsipper (1.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Delete in Contacts no longer rebuilds every row. The matching
    Adw.ExpanderRow is now removed from the listbox directly and the
    JSON save is deferred to the next idle slot, so the confirmation
    dialog disappears and the row vanishes in the same frame.
  * Drop the maximize / fullscreen button from the headerbar window
    controls; the tall dialer pane never benefits from fullscreen.
    Resize-by-drag is unchanged.

